Jahshaka patch 0074 — the cascade continuation composites the transmittance ONCE,
and the bounce-injection walk carries its cone across a hop.

MEDIA-only patch (two Hlms/compute pieces:
`Samples/Media/Hlms/Pbs/Any/Vct_piece_ps.any` and
`Samples/Media/VCT/LightVctBounceInject_piece_cs.any`). THE PROCESS COST IS
STATED RATHER THAN AVOIDED: Studio stages its media from the SOURCE tree
(cmake/IncludeOgre.cmake), so every tree must still reset its ogre-next submodule
and re-run `irisgl/scripts/build-ogre.sh` — no engine recompile beyond the
staging. It OVERLAPS patches 0021, 0033, 0045, 0048, 0066 and 0070 in the pixel
piece and 0060/0070 in the compute piece, so a tree that already carries those
hits `build-ogre.sh`'s "Upstream changed the patched file" on a re-run: that is
the documented per-patch reverse-check blind spot and NOT an upstream change. The
cure is the recorded one — `git -C irisgl/thirdparty/ogre-next checkout -- . &&
git -C irisgl/thirdparty/ogre-next clean -fd` and re-run the script.

WHY (Jahshaka lane PHOTON-M1, 2026-09-17, measured; the 2026-09-17 render audit's
PHOTON F8 and F9 named both).

(1) THE DOUBLE TRANSMITTANCE (F9), in both continuations of the pixel piece and
    in the compute twin. `voxelConeTraceDiff`/`voxelConeTraceSpec` start their
    opacity accumulator at `startingAlpha` — the caller's own `result.alpha` —
    and weight every sample they composite by `a = 1 - alpha` from that start.
    What a continuation RETURNS is therefore already reduced by the light the
    cone used up in the cascades before it. The composite then multiplied by
    `( 1.0 - result.alpha )` a SECOND time, so every outer cascade contributed
    (1-A0)^2 of its radiance. Upstream calls that second factor
    "de-amplification" (`OgreVctCascadedVoxelizer.cpp:470-486`) and pairs it with
    "more bounces for coarser cascades": both halves are a brightness
    stabilisation invented when the opacity was DOUBLING at every hop — which
    Jahshaka patch 0033 fixed at the cause. With 0033 in, the factor is a pure
    darkening of every cascade past the first.

(2) THE COMPUTE WALK STOPPED AFTER ONE HOP (F8). The bounce-injection twin of
    `computeVctProbe` still had the two defects the pixel piece had before 0033
    and 0066: `result.alpha += newRes.alpha` DOUBLED the opacity at every hop (the
    accumulator already started at `result.alpha`), so the loop's `< 0.95f` guard
    ended the walk after one cascade and a bounce never travelled further than
    cascade 1; and the cone's AGE restarted at every hop, so the continuation
    marched the next cascade at a footprint that never matched the cone's solid
    angle. `VctResult` gains `travelled` and the trace a `startingTravelled`, in
    the new cascade's units by the same directional scale 0066 uses.

WHAT IT DOES NOT TOUCH. A single fitted volume never hops: the chain-OFF picture
of the default scene is byte-identical across this patch
(sha256 7407fff2ded7f6462fb2ca3f23f11d292484b6395d56931922814132a25a5799,
measured both sides). The lightless-slab suite `gi.chain_face` is bit-identical
too — the composite multiplies a radiance the slab does not have, and the
ambient/escape term the slab measures is not on this path.

MEASURED (PHOTON-M1, Xvfb 1920x1080, fixed 1/60 s clock, probes read "plain"
= linear radiance, frames never wall clock):

  * the default scene's selftest picture, F9 alone: 10,686 of 65,536 pixels move,
    max 1/255, every changed channel BRIGHTER (32,053 channels up, 0 down);
    the compute walk on top of it moves a further 4,590, max 1/255, all brighter.
  * Showroom 2 at High (one bounce, so F9 alone): the chain's cones read
    74.4583 -> 75.0694 mean probe (+0.82 %) against a single fitted volume's
    91.3056, which is unchanged to the digit — the chain-vs-single darkening
    SEAM-1 measured as 12.5 % (18.45 % on this tree) falls to 17.78 %.
  * a closed cube room of albedo 0.79 at Epic (three bounces): the light each
    extra bounce pass adds, as a fraction of the one-bounce picture, rises from
    6.09 / 1.23 / 1.97 % to 9.26 / 1.77 / 3.35 % — the bounce reaches past
    cascade 1 for the first time.
